.TH NULL 4 "February 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "Device Drivers Manual"
.SH NAME
null \- the null device
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /dev/null
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B null
character device discards all bytes written to it and returns end-of-file on read.
.PP
Reads always return
.B 0
(EOF).
Writes always succeed and return the requested byte count.
.PP
.BR lseek (2)
operations succeed and update file offsets, but offsets do not affect device behavior.
.PP
.BR poll (2)
reports
.B POLLOUT
as ready and does not report
.BR POLLIN .
.BR ioctl (2)
is not supported.
.PP
.BR mmap (2)
is not supported for
.BR /dev/null .
.SH FILES
.B /dev/null
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ENOTTY
Any
.BR ioctl (2)
request.
.TP
.B EINVAL
Any
.BR mmap (2)
attempt.
.SH EXAMPLES
Discard command output:
.PP
.nf
    $ echo "hi" > /dev/null
.fi
.PP
Read EOF immediately:
.PP
.nf
    $ cat /dev/null
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR full (4),
.BR zero (4),
.BR poll (2),
.BR mmap (2)
